---
import OnePage from '../layouts/OnePage.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { brand } from '../data/brand';

const domainDisplay = brand.url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');

const title = `Terms of Use | ${brand.name}`;
const description = `The terms that govern access to and use of this website, operated by ${brand.name} and ${brand.company.name}.`;
---

<OnePage title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <section class="legal" aria-labelledby="terms-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 id="terms-h">Terms of Use</h1>

      <p>
        These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern your access to and use of {domainDisplay} (the
        "Website"), including its articles, downloads, booking functions, products and services.
      </p>

      <p>
        The Website is the personal website of Ella Siew, jointly operated by Ella Siew and{' '}
        {brand.company.name} ("we", "us" or "our"). Unless a checkout page, proposal, order form
        or service agreement expressly identifies another seller, {brand.company.name} is the
        contracting provider for paid products and services purchased through or following use of
        the Website.
      </p>

      <p>
        By using the Website, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the
        Website. Additional terms shown at checkout or contained in a signed proposal, order form
        or service agreement apply to the relevant purchase. If there is a conflict, the more
        specific transaction document prevails for that transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>1. About the Website</h2>
      <p>
        The Website presents Ella Siew's professional profile, insights and services concerning
        personal branding, AI visibility, AI SEO/GEO, LinkedIn presence, digital authority and
        related topics. It may allow you to read or download content, contact us, book
        consultations, subscribe to communications and purchase products or services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Website content is general information. It is not legal, financial, investment, medical
        or other regulated professional advice and should not be relied upon as such. You should
        obtain appropriate independent advice for your circumstances.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Eligibility and authority</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old and legally capable of entering into a contract to make
        a purchase. If you use the Website for an organisation, you confirm that you have
        authority to act for it and that the organisation accepts these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Bookings and consultations</h2>
      <p>
        Bookings are handled through Cal.com. Available times are not guaranteed until the
        booking is confirmed.
      </p>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate booking information and attend at the confirmed time.
        Rescheduling, cancellation, lateness and no-show rules displayed during booking form part
        of the booking terms. A free or introductory consultation does not create an ongoing
        advisory, agency, fiduciary or client relationship and does not oblige either party to
        enter into a paid engagement.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may decline, cancel or reschedule a consultation where reasonably necessary, including
        because of availability, conflict, safety, suspected misuse or circumstances beyond our
        reasonable control. If we cancel a prepaid consultation and do not provide a suitable
        alternative, the amount paid for that consultation will be refunded, subject to applicable
        law.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Purchases and contract formation</h2>
      <p>
        Before you pay, the applicable product page, checkout, proposal or order form should
        state the seller, material description, price, currency, taxes or additional charges,
        billing frequency, delivery or access timing, cancellation and refund terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Submitting an order is an offer to purchase. A contract is formed when we accept the order
        by issuing confirmation or beginning performance, unless the checkout states otherwise. We
        may reject or cancel an order before acceptance for reasons such as pricing or description
        error, suspected fraud, unavailability, legal restrictions or inability to supply. If
        payment has been taken for a rejected order, it will be returned using an appropriate
        method.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for providing correct billing, contact and delivery information and
        for ensuring that your payment method is authorised.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Services</h2>
      <p>
        The precise scope, deliverables, timetable, client responsibilities, fees, revision limits
        and acceptance criteria for consulting or implementation services must be set out in a
        proposal, order form or service agreement. The Website alone does not promise a
        particular project scope.
      </p>
      <p>
        You agree to provide timely, accurate information, access, approvals and materials
        reasonably required for the work. Delays or omissions by you may affect schedules and
        results. Changes outside the agreed scope may require revised fees and timing, subject to
        your approval.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will provide services with reasonable care and skill. Unless expressly guaranteed in a
        signed agreement, we do not guarantee search rankings, AI citations, audience growth,
        leads, revenue, media exposure, LinkedIn performance or any other particular commercial
        result. Search engines, AI platforms, social networks and third-party algorithms are
        outside our control and may change without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Digital products, downloads and content access</h2>
      <p>
        Digital products may include guides, templates, recordings, courses, reports or other
        downloadable or online materials. The relevant product page will describe the access
        method, included content and any access period.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unless expressly stated otherwise, a purchase gives you a limited, personal or
        internal-business, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the purchased
        materials. You may not resell, sublicense, publish, share access credentials, distribute
        substantial copies, remove ownership notices or use the materials to create a competing
        product.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Prices, payment and recurring charges</h2>
      <p>
        Prices and accepted payment methods are shown at checkout. You must pay all disclosed
        amounts in the stated currency. You are responsible for taxes or charges identified before
        purchase, except taxes imposed on our income.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will not impose a recurring subscription unless the checkout clearly states the billing
        frequency, renewal terms, price and cancellation method before you agree. Where recurring
        billing applies, you authorise the payment provider to charge the selected method
        according to those disclosed terms until cancellation takes effect.
      </p>
      <p>
        Payment processing may be supplied by a third party under its own terms. We are not
        responsible for a payment provider's independent service failure, but this does not
        remove any responsibility that applicable law places on us as seller.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Cancellations and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        The cancellation and refund policy disclosed on the relevant product page, booking page,
        checkout, proposal or order form applies to that purchase. Review it before paying.
        Different services and digital products may have different rules because preparation,
        reserved time, delivery and access conditions differ.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms excludes a refund, cancellation right or other remedy that cannot
        lawfully be excluded. If no specific policy was displayed, contact{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>; we will assess the request fairly having
        regard to whether performance began, resources were committed, digital access was supplied
        and applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not state that all purchases are non-refundable unless that rule is specifically
        disclosed before purchase and is lawful in the buyer's location.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your content and permissions</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of materials you submit. You grant us a limited permission to host,
        copy, adapt and use those materials only as reasonably necessary to respond to you,
        provide contracted services, process a purchase, maintain records and exercise our legal
        rights.
      </p>
      <p>
        You confirm that you have the necessary rights to provide the materials and that our
        authorised use will not infringe another person's rights. We will not publish your name,
        testimonial, logo, case study or confidential client material for promotional purposes
        without appropriate permission.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Website and its original text, design, graphics, branding, downloads, methods and
        other content are owned by or licensed to Ella Siew or {brand.company.name} and are
        protected by applicable intellectual-property laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may view the Website and make limited copies for personal, non-commercial reference.
        You may not reproduce, republish, sell, scrape, systematically extract, modify, distribute
        or exploit Website content without prior written permission, except where law permits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Short quotations may be used with clear attribution and a link to the source where
        permitted by law. Names, logos and branding may not be used in a way that suggests
        endorsement or affiliation without permission.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the Website unlawfully, fraudulently or to harm another person;</li>
        <li>interfere with security, availability, servers or networks;</li>
        <li>introduce malware, malicious code or automated abuse;</li>
        <li>attempt unauthorised access to accounts, systems or data;</li>
        <li>submit false, misleading, infringing, defamatory or harmful content;</li>
        <li>harvest personal data or send unsolicited communications;</li>
        <li>bypass access, payment or usage restrictions; or</li>
        <li>use Website content or services in a manner that violates another person's rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may restrict access where reasonably necessary to protect the Website, users, our rights or legal compliance.</p>

      <h2>12. Third-party services and links</h2>
      <p>
        The Website uses Cal.com for booking and Google Fonts for typography, and may link to
        social networks, payment providers and other third-party services in future. We do not
        control their independent content, availability, security or practices. A link does not
        necessarily mean endorsement. Your use of a third-party service may be governed by its own
        terms and privacy notice.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        Information submitted through a general contact form or introductory consultation should
        not be treated as subject to a professional privilege or comprehensive confidentiality
        obligation unless we have signed an agreement that provides otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once a client engagement begins, confidentiality obligations will be governed by the
        applicable proposal, order form, nondisclosure agreement or service agreement. We will
        nevertheless handle personal data in accordance with our Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep Website content useful and accurate, but content may be general, incomplete
        or become outdated. To the extent permitted by law, the Website is provided on an
        "as available" basis without a guarantee of uninterrupted access, error-free operation or
        suitability for every purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Examples, educational materials and past outcomes do not guarantee future results. You
        remain responsible for your business, publishing, marketing, investment and implementation
        decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms excludes an express commitment in a signed agreement or a statutory
        obligation that cannot lawfully be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, neither Ella Siew nor {brand.company.name} will
        be liable for indirect or consequential loss, loss of profits, revenue, opportunity,
        goodwill or data arising from use of the Website or general free content.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a paid purchase, any limitation or allocation of liability in the applicable proposal,
        order form or service agreement will apply. Where no specific agreement applies, our
        aggregate liability arising from that purchase will not exceed the amount you paid for the
        affected product or service, except to the extent such a limitation is prohibited by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms limits liability for fraud, fraudulent misrepresentation, wilful
        misconduct, or any death, personal injury, consumer right or other liability that cannot
        lawfully be limited or excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Indemnity for misuse</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, you agree to be responsible for reasonable losses, claims
        and costs arising from your unlawful misuse of the Website, infringement of another
        person's rights, or material breach of these Terms. This clause does not apply to the
        extent the loss was caused by our own breach or wrongdoing and does not reduce any
        non-excludable consumer right.
      </p>

      <h2>17. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle personal data. It forms
        part of the Website information but does not replace any separate data-processing terms
        required for a client project.
      </p>

      <h2>18. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Website at any time. We may suspend or terminate access where you
        materially breach these Terms, fail to pay an undisputed amount, threaten security or
        legal compliance, or misuse content or services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Termination does not affect accrued payment obligations, rights or provisions intended to
        survive, including intellectual property, confidentiality, liability and dispute
        provisions. Treatment of prepaid fees will remain subject to the purchase terms and
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>19. Changes to the Website and Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update the Website and these Terms to reflect service, operational or legal
        changes. The current Terms will be posted on this page. Changes will not retroactively
        alter an accepted purchase or signed agreement unless permitted by that agreement or
        required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>20. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and non-contractual disputes relating to the Website are governed by the laws
        of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, without regard to conflict-of-law
        principles.
      </p>
      <p>
        The courts of Hong Kong have non-exclusive jurisdiction. This does not remove any
        mandatory consumer protection or right to bring proceedings that applies in your place of
        residence and cannot lawfully be waived.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before commencing formal proceedings, you and we should first attempt in good faith to
        resolve the dispute by written notice, unless urgent relief is required.
      </p>

      <h2>21. General</h2>
      <p>
        If a provision is unlawful or unenforceable, it will be limited or removed to the minimum
        extent necessary and the remaining provisions will continue. A failure to enforce a
        provision is not a waiver. You may not transfer your rights or obligations without our
        consent; we may transfer ours as part of a genuine reorganisation, business transfer or
        assignment that does not unlawfully reduce your rights.
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and any applicable checkout terms, proposal,
        order form or service agreement, constitute the relevant agreement for the matters they
        cover.
      </p>

      <h2>22. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms, an order or a service may be sent to:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Ella Siew and {brand.company.name}</strong><br />
        Website: {domainDisplay}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</OnePage>
